+## 1. ENUMERATION VERDICT
+
+Full receipt: **`r58-evidence/10-memtypes.txt`** (raw: `r58-evidence/vulkaninfo-memprops-raw.txt`).
+Sources: `vulkaninfo` VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties (device creation only, no allocation), and the
+pre-existing R51 lane-240 `GGML_VK_ALLOC_TRACE=1` load at
+`C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r51-spill-wt/r51-evidence/30-planorder.txt`. They agree line for line, so
+**deliverable 1 needed no load cell** — it is complete despite the box being owned by chain138.
+
+**Heaps:** 0 = 21.07 GiB `DEVICE_LOCAL`; 1 = 10.54 GiB (no flags); 2 = 256 MiB `DEVICE_LOCAL`.
+
+**16 memory types are enumerated, but every storage buffer we create reports
+`memoryTypeBits = 0xf`** (46 of 46 allocations in the R51 trace). Only types 0–3 are eligible at
+all; types 4–15, including every AMD `DEVICE_COHERENT`/`DEVICE_UNCACHED` variant and the 8–15
+mirrors, can never hold our weights.
+
+> **Beyond the reservation there are exactly TWO usable memory types:**
+> **type 1** — `HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT` (uncached / write-combined), and
+> **type 3** — `HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED`. Both on heap 1.
+
+**Where today's split lands, and why — it is enumeration order, not a measurement.**
+`ggml_vk_placement_attempts()` (`:5207`, UMA branch) offers three required-flag passes:
+
+1. `DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT` → matches only types 2/6/10/14, **all on the 256 MiB
+   heap 2**. Structurally dead for GiB-sized weight blocks (it is alive for the small KV tensors,
+   which is exactly why those land in type 2).
+2. `DEVICE_LOCAL` → types 0/4/8/12 on heap 0, until heap 0 is full.
+3. `HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT` → types **1 and 3** on heap 1. `ggml_vk_find_memory_properties()`
+   (`:4599`) walks types in **ascending index**, and the planner deduplicates keeping the **first**
+   position (`:19925`), so **type 1 beats type 3 because 1 < 3**. Nothing measured it.
+
+Type 3 is not speculative: the driver already serves it on this box for the staging/transfer
+buffers. It has simply never carried weights.
+
+**Correctness argument (stronger than "placement doesn't change arithmetic"):** both eligible
+heap-1 types carry `HOST_COHERENT`, so moving the split between them adds no flush/invalidate
+obligation and no new coherence code. The same shader reads the same bytes.
+
