+## 2. What was written
+
+### 2.1 Probe — `test-backend-ops memtype` (`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`)
+
+`test-backend-ops memtype [--bytes N] [--rounds R] [--types 1,3]` (default 4 GiB, 3 rounds, every
+eligible type). Per type it prints one canonical line:
+
+```
+ggml_vulkan memtype-probe v1: type=T heap=H flags=0xF bytes=B gpu_read_gbs=X cpu_memcpy_gbs=Y
+```
+
+Design:
+
+* **What is timed is the real path.** An f16 `MUL_MAT` with `n=1` — the same mat-vec a plain decode
+  token runs — built as an ordinary ggml graph on the ordinary Vulkan backend. Not a hand-wired
+  pipeline, so it cannot drift away from what the engine does.
+* **Placement is pinned** with `ggml_vk_memtype_force(t)`, which sets a process-global that
+  `ggml_vk_find_memory_properties()` honours. That predicate is the single seam both the direct
+  candidate walk and the batch planner call, so one filter covers both paths. Production leaves it
+  at `-1` and the loop is byte-for-byte the one that shipped.
+* **Eligibility is measured, not assumed.** `ggml_vk_memtype_buffer_info()` returns the real
+  `VkMemoryRequirements::memoryTypeBits` for a storage buffer; types outside it are skipped with a
+  printed reason instead of being timed as placements that cannot happen.
+* **Chunking is explicit.** `max_buffer_size` on this device is 2 GiB, so the span is split into
+  chunks of at most `min(suballocation_block_size, max_buffer_size)`, rounded to whole 4096-wide
+  f16 rows, and the receipt prints the chunking it used. A refusal prints
+  `memtype T: REFUSED - no room for N B` and returns 0 — a type whose heap cannot hold the span is
+  a result, not a failure.
+* **One discarded warm-up round** before the timed rounds (first compute compiles pipelines and
+  fills descriptor pools), then best-of-`R`. The CPU `memcpy` of the same span is timed the same way.
+
+**Exact HQ command lines** (quiet window, one at a time, `Get-Process llama-server,llama-cli,llama-bench,test-backend-ops` empty first):
+
+```
+# the two beyond-reservation types, 4 GiB each — the measurement this lane exists for
+build-vulkan\bin\test-backend-ops.exe memtype --types 1 --bytes 4294967296 --rounds 3 > r58-evidence/40-probe-type1.txt
+build-vulkan\bin\test-backend-ops.exe memtype --types 3 --bytes 4294967296 --rounds 3 > r58-evidence/41-probe-type3.txt
+
+# the device-local reference number (heap 0) — what "at bus speed" means on this box today
+build-vulkan\bin\test-backend-ops.exe memtype --types 0 --bytes 4294967296 --rounds 3 > r58-evidence/42-probe-type0.txt
+
+# everything eligible in one pass, if a single quiet slot is all there is
+build-vulkan\bin\test-backend-ops.exe memtype --bytes 4294967296 --rounds 3 > r58-evidence/43-probe-all.txt
+```
+
+Concatenate the winning receipts into one file and point `GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE` at it to use
+`auto`.
+
+### 2.2 Allocator change (`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp`)
+
+| What | Where | Note |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GGML_VK_HOST_SPLIT_MEMTYPE` / `_CACHED` / `GGML_VK_MEMTYPE_PROBE_FILE` parsing, and the canonical probe-line format + its parser | `:4426-4536` (`ggml_vk_host_split_auto_type()` `:4439`, `ggml_vk_host_split_memtype()` `:4496`, `ggml_vk_host_split_cached()` `:4520`) | Parsed **once per process**. Writer and reader of the receipt line live in the same TU so they cannot drift. |
+| Probe-only memory-type pin | `:4542` (`vk_memtype_forced`) + the filter at `:4605-4608` | `-1` in every served run. |
+| The reorder | `:19800-19855` (`ggml_vk_host_split_prefer()`), called at `:19945` | Reorders **only among host-split candidate positions**; device-local candidates keep their exact position. Host-split candidates are deliberately **not** assumed contiguous — under `GGML_VK_PREFER_HOST_MEMORY` the policy puts them first, and a naive rotate would shift device-local candidates. |
+| Per-buffer receipt | `:20022-20035` | One ungated stderr line per host-split buffer naming type, heap, flags, bytes and the preference in force. |
+| Probe hooks | `:24508-24566` (`ggml_vk_memtype_force` `:24508`, `_enumerate`, `_buffer_info`, `_probe_line` `:24560`) | `GGML_BACKEND_API` inside the existing `extern "C"` test-seam block. |
+
+**Default is `legacy`: with nothing set, not one byte of placement changes.** A preference that is
+unavailable, out of range, or unparsable prints one stderr line and falls through to the legacy
+order — it never turns a working load into a hard failure (the same principle the bulk-large-heap
+fallback already states at `:5196`).
